# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# For a zero-setup run against the committed fixture league, you need none of
# this: `uv run poe demo` sets FFMCP_MODE=demo for you.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# live = talk to ESPN and Sleeper. demo = committed fixtures, no network.
FFMCP_MODE=live

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# League (required when FFMCP_MODE=live)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# From your league URL:
# https://fantasy.espn.com/football/league?leagueId=1234567
FFMCP_LEAGUE_ID=

# Defaults to the current NFL season when unset.
# FFMCP_SEASON=2026

# Which team is yours. If unset, the server asks once (via MCP elicitation)
# and caches the answer. Set it to skip the prompt.
#FFMCP_TEAM_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials — PRIVATE LEAGUES ONLY. Public leagues need neither.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are session cookies for your ESPN account. They are as sensitive as a
# password: anyone holding them can act as you on espn.com. They cannot be
# fetched programmatically.
#
# To find them: log in at fantasy.espn.com, open DevTools (F12) ->
# Application/Storage -> Cookies -> https://fantasy.espn.com, and copy the
# `espn_s2` and `SWID` values.
#
# SWID includes the surrounding braces, e.g. {1A2B3C4D-...}
FFMCP_ESPN_S2=
FFMCP_SWID={}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Betting lines (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A free key from https://the-odds-api.com (500 requests/month; the server uses
# about 120 a month). Adds each player's team implied total as context. Without
# it, everything else works and the "Game:" line is simply absent.
# FFMCP_ODDS_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP deployment — required for --transport streamable-http in live mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed for stdio (Claude Desktop/Code), and not needed for FFMCP_MODE=demo
# (that mode serves only synthetic fixtures, so an open demo endpoint is harmless).
#
# Every request to a live-mode HTTP server must send this back as
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, or the server rejects it with 401. Without
# it, anyone who finds the URL could read your real league. Generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
FFMCP_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tuning
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FFMCP_CACHE_DIR=~/.cache/ffmcp
# FFMCP_SIMS=10000
